<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">
    <!--
        Diagnostic server actions for the DAADit Mistral provider.

        This file is NO LONGER referenced from __manifest__.py — Odoo 19's
        safe-eval refuses ``code`` blocks that contain IMPORT_NAME or
        IMPORT_FROM opcodes (i.e. any ``import`` / ``from … import`` line),
        which broke the original introspection actions at install time.

        It's kept here only so that re-listing it in the manifest doesn't
        revive the old broken records. The introspection job is now done by
        ``services/diagnostics.py`` (UserError trace tap) and the
        register-hook bytecode scans in the model files, which don't run
        through safe-eval and therefore have no opcode restrictions.

        If you ever need to re-introduce a server-action diagnostic, write
        it without ``import`` statements — ``UserError`` is exposed in the
        action's eval namespace as ``UserError`` directly.
    -->
</odoo>
